+{
+  "class_id": 2290,
+  "title": "gitreins-worktree-guard-full-suite-shared-db-flake-wave-contention",
+  "description": "gitreins-worktree-guard-full-suite-shared-db-flake-wave-contention",
+  "created_at": "2026-09-25 03:28:37",
+  "answers": [
+    {
+      "answer_id": 2485,
+      "language": "go",
+      "environment": "docker",
+      "version": "latest",
+      "solution": "The solution is written and verified. Full document at `/workspace/solution/SOLUTION.md`.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe wedge is a chain of four independent faults, not one bug:\n\n1. **Unscoped Tier-1** — guard never inspects the staged file list, so docs/asset commits run the full DB-backed suite.\n2. **Shared mutable DB** — every worktree uses the same `dexdat_test`; sibling suites mutate bootstrap/admin rows concurrently.\n3. **Timeout vs. contention** — 300 s can't cover the full suite under contention, so the guard trips fail-open.\n4. **Verdict/exit mismatch** — the guard prints `DEGRADED PASS ... allowed`, but the hook exits non-zero because nothing maps `DEGRADED_PASS → 0`. Workers therefore retry forever.\n\n## Fix (five drop-in changes)\n\n| # | Change | Fixes |\n|---|--------|-------|\n| 1 | Path-scoped short-circuit: non-Python diff → `SKIP`, never spawn pytest | zero-Python wedge |\n| 2 | Per-worktree DB `dexdat_test_<worktree>` exported via `DEXDAT_TEST_DSN` | sibling contention |\n| 3 | Scoped test selection (`impacted()` / `--testmon`) | timeout |\n| 4 | Explicit guard exit contract: `0=PASS`, `1=FAIL`, `2=DEGRADED_PASS`; hook maps `2→exit 0` | the \"lie\" + infinite retry |\n| 5 | Bounded, classified worker retry as defense-in-depth | livelock |\n| 6 | Advisory-lock + rollback fixtures for the three flaky tests | flaky fixtures |\n\n## Verification (executed)\n\n- Unit: `12 passed` — covers empty/docs-only → `skip`, Python/manifest → `run`, and critically `hook_exit(2) == 0`.\n- End-to-end: temporary git repos with the real `pre-commit` hook and injected fake guards:\n  - `guard_pass` → exit 0\n  - `guard_degraded` → **exit 0** (previously aborted)\n  - `guard_hard_fail` → exit 1\n  - docs-only diff → `skip`, Python diff → `run`\n  - `ALL E2E CHECKS PASSED`\n\nArtifacts together: `fix/gitreins_scope.py`, `fix/tier1-guard.sh`, `fix/pre-commit`, `verify/test_gitreins_scope.py`, `verify/e2e_hook_check.sh`, plus the wave acceptance checklist in §4.3 of the doc.\n",
+      "evidence": "# Evidence\n- Problem class: gitreins-worktree-guard-full-suite-shared-db-flake-wave-contention\n- Model: openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash\n- Solved: 2026-09-25T03:28:37.730Z\n- Verification: solution produced by pi in sandbox; see signatures.json\n",
+      "signatures": {
+        "description": "In wave dispatch (one worker per git worktree), each worker Tier-1 guard runs the FULL pytest suite against the shared dexdat_test DB (conftest default localhost:5435). Under sibling concurrency the suite exceeds the 300s guard timeout or fails on the documented batched-DB-contention fixture tests (test_list_contexts_filter_by_type, test_first_user_admin_reaches_admin_gated_endpoint, test_admin_bootstrap_dangling), so commits wedge even when the diff contains zero Python files. Also: guard DEGRADED PASS with hook_timeout says commit allowed to proceed (fail-open) but the pre-commit hook still aborts, so the message lies and the worker retries forever.",
